const e="indradhanushya-maharashtra-youth-festival",h=2023,t="Read from the whole 16-page Guidelines for the Indradhanushya: Maharashtra State Inter-University Youth Festival (the 2023 edition, published on the DBATU site). Placed: eligibility (every point), disqualification, contingent size and officials, identity cards, flags, travel, food and lodging, conduct and discipline, the time-limit rule, the registration and document rules, fees (pro-rata and caution money), the selection rounds inside each university, and all rules, time limits, team sizes, accompanists, evaluation qualities and required documents for each of the 27 template events. Short Film and Procession are not in the template and are named under 'other' with their rules. The guidelines do NOT print: the festival dates, the host university, venue or address, contact people or numbers, prizes or trophies for any event except that the Short Film gets First, Second and Third prizes (no amounts), points, grades or ranks, marks or weights (only the qualities judged), complaints or appeal steps beyond telling the Organizing Secretary and the Chairman, or any news item. These stay empty. The PDF jumps from section (6) to (11) and from (13) to (20). The calendar, dates and schedule in points (8), (9) and (10), the list of documents in (19) and sections (7) to (10) and (14) to (19) are not in the file and could not be read. The Registration dates (24 to 31 October), the pro-rata deadline (10 October) and the amounts are printed without a year, so they are kept as Variables. Two numbers disagree inside the file: Other Rules point 2 says Rs. 1000 refundable caution money for each team, and Guidelines point 17 says Rs. 2000. Both are written in the CautionMoney Variable. The contingent strength is 'maximum 50 per University', but the table of contingent details totals 55 (49 students and accompanists plus officials); both are written. The template uses two groups, Solo and Team, instead of age groups; the guidelines print no age band other than the under-25 limit.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Indradhanushya: Maharashtra State Inter-University Youth Festival. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Only bonafide full-time students under 25 years of age on {{AgeCutoffDate}} can take part. Online registration is open {{RegistrationPeriod}}. Every university sends its team with a team manager, and a lady team manager is a must if girls take part.","Notes":["Each performance has a minimum and a maximum time. Going over the maximum, or under the minimum, means disqualification. There is a grace period of 15 seconds for the maximum time only.","Do not reveal the name of the student, the accompanist or the university during the event. Doing so means disqualification."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The host university runs the competitions for all participating universities.","The events are in six sections: Music, Dance, Literary, Theatre, Fine Arts, and the Short Film and Procession.","Music events: Indian Classical Vocal, Indian Classical Instrumental Percussion (Taalvadya), Indian Classical Instrumental Non-Percussion (Swarvadya), Natyasangeet Vocal, Indian Light Vocal, Indian Group Song, Folk Orchestra, Western Vocal, Western Instrumental, Western Group Song.","Dance events: Indian Classical Dance and Indian Folk Dance. Literary events: Elocution, Debate and Quiz. Theatre events: Mimicry, One Act Play, Skit and Mime.","Fine Arts events: Painting, Collage, Poster Making, Clay Modeling, Cartooning, Rangoli, Spot Photography and Installation.","Each participant carries an identity card with a photograph, signed by the proper authority of the university.","The contingent leader gives the university flag to the host university at registration. The host flies all flags at a strategic place. The university collects the flag from the Registration Desk after the prize distribution ceremony.","Each participating university gives the responsibility for the festival to its Director, Students' Development or Welfare.","Bring enough warm bedding, blankets, woollen clothes, medicines and locks. It is advised that participants and officials are vaccinated against Covid, cholera, typhoid and similar diseases.","The festival is part of the National Integration Camp scheme, so a university may use the railway concession.","All student participants must attend the Procession and the Inaugural Ceremony."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Only a bonafide full-time student can take part. The student must be enrolled for a degree, a post-graduate degree or a diploma course of at least one academic year, whose examination is held by the University after passing the 12th class examination or an equal examination.","A student of an open university is a bonafide student and can take part if the other conditions are met.","A student in a correspondence course in an institute or centre of the university, a casual student, an external student and a student in a bridge course cannot take part.","Only a student who is less than 25 years of age on {{AgeCutoffDate}} of the academic year in which the festival is held can take part.","Not more than 7 years may pass after the student passed the examination that qualified him or her for first admission to a UG degree or diploma course of an affiliated college, constituent college, recognized institute or academic department of the university.","A student can take part for 1 year more than the normal length of the course. A student in a three-year course (B.A., B.Sc., B.Com. and similar) can take part for four years. A student in a four-year course (B.E., B.Tech. and similar) can take part for five years.","A student cannot represent more than one university in one academic year.","Provisional admission to a course of a university or college does not make a student eligible.","A student who moves from one university to another is eligible only after the admission in the new university is regularized and the new university admits him or her as a bonafide student.","A participant who is not eligible is disqualified from the festival. Disqualification for ineligibility can mean that the participant and the event are scratched for three academic years, including the current one.","Each participating university must make sure that every participant is eligible."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Complete the online registration and give all details correctly, without mistakes.","The Team Managers give all the required documents to the Registration Desk as per the schedule that the Organizing Secretary of the host university sends. A participant whose documents are not submitted is disqualified.","Each university sends a Team Manager (male) and a Team Manager (female). A lady Team Manager is a must if the contingent has girl participants. At most two persons are sent as contingent in-charge or Team Managers, and they stay in touch with the Organizing Committee of the host university.","A university that takes part in the Short Film event gives its film at the Registration Desk during registration.","At each event venue, give the required documents to the Event In-charge 20 minutes before the event starts. Write your Slot No. on them. Do not write the name of the university or of the participants on them. The Event In-charge gives them to the judges at the time of the performance.","The documents for each event (three copies of each) are listed in the event rules."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["Online registration: {{RegistrationPeriod}}.","The pro-rata fee is paid on or before {{ProRataDeadline}}.","The Travel Plan is sent to the host university {{TravelPlanNotice}}.","The Procession is held on the first day, before the Inaugural Ceremony.","Food from the host university starts on the afternoon of the day before the festival begins. It lasts until dinner on the last day.","Each university must follow the calendar, dates and schedule of the festival, as sent by the host university."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Deposits","Items":["Each participating university pays a pro-rata amount: {{ProRataAmount}}.","Each university gives a refundable caution money at registration: {{CautionMoney}}. The cost of any loss of stores, or damage to property that was issued and not returned, is cut from it. The university collects the money from the Registration Desk after the formalities."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Travel, Food and Lodging","Items":["The participating university pays the travel expenses of the whole contingent from its place to the host university. It also pays the food expenses of the whole contingent during the journey.","The host university gives free boarding and lodging for the festival. Students may be housed as guests in student hostels, common rooms and similar places.","The host university gives food from the afternoon of the day before the festival begins until dinner on the last day."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Contingent","Items":["The contingent is at most 50 persons for each university. {{ContingentSize}}.","Accompanists should preferably be students, and they get participation certificates. Outsiders may be allowed if suitable students are not available.","Universities must not bring any extra person. No extra person is allowed at any cost."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Selection Inside the University","Items":["The participating university sends the rules and the calendar of the festival to all its affiliated colleges, constituent colleges, recognized institutes and academic departments.","The university holds a District or Zone-wise Inter-Collegiate, Inter-Institute or Inter-Department Youth Festival, and appeals to all its colleges, institutes and departments to take part in large numbers.","The university also holds a University Level Youth Festival for the winners of the District or Zone-wise festival.","The university decides the modalities, rules and schedule of these festivals and tells all its colleges, institutes and departments in advance.","The university selects the students for the Indradhanushya from the District or Zone-wise festival and the University Level festival. It sets a special way to select them and tells all colleges, institutes and departments in advance.","The university holds mentoring sessions for the selected students and invites experts in the areas to mentor them.","The university makes a special provision in its budget for the District or Zone-wise festival, the University Level festival, the selection of students, their mentoring and the participation in the Indradhanushya."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Discipline","Items":["The use of fireworks or arms is strictly prohibited. If one is unavoidable for a cultural performance, an imitation can be used with the prior permission of the Organizing Secretary.","No official or member of the participating or host universities may go to the press or media on any controversial issue.","Drinking liquor, eve teasing, influencing the adjudicators and indecent behaviour inside the campus and the venue are strictly prohibited.","If the behaviour of a contingent is against the aims of the Indradhanushya, the host university can take suitable action against the members. An individual or a team can be debarred for three academic years, including the current one.","Anyone who breaks these rules can face disciplinary action, up to debarring the whole university team.","The Contingent Leaders are responsible for the discipline of their contingent. They and their members follow all the instructions of the Organizing Secretary, and all participants follow the instructions of the host university.","Do not reveal the identity of the student participants, accompanists or the participating university during the event. If a participant, an accompanist or any member of the contingent does so during the performance, that participant is disqualified from the event."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Time Limits","Items":["The time starts immediately after the final announcement by the organizers. For One Act Play and Skit, the time starts as soon as the announcement starts or the curtain is fully open, whichever is earlier.","Each participant must keep to the minimum and the maximum time of the performance. A participant who finishes before the minimum time, or goes over the maximum time, is disqualified from the event.","There is a grace period of 15 seconds to finish within the maximum time. There is no grace period for the minimum time."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Problems and Complaints","Items":["For any problem with accommodation, cleanliness, venues, food, water, electricity, safety and security or rehearsal venues, the Team Managers tell the Organizing Secretary or the Chairman of the Oversee Committee.","In a medical emergency, the member of the contingent contacts the In-charge of the First Aid Assistance Committee, the Organizing Secretary, or the Chairman or members of the Oversee Committee.","If any indiscipline happens, the Contingent Leaders talk to the participants and tell the Organizing Secretary at once.","Serious matters are brought to the notice of the Vice-Chancellor of the host university and the Chairman of the Observer Committee."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Events","Items":["Short Film (group event, not in this template): each university submits one short film on any subject at the Registration Desk. Students act in all roles. There is no limit on the number of students for acting and making the film. The film must have a story, and a documentary is not accepted. The university must get the Censor Certificate. The content, dialogue, lyrics and music must not hurt the feelings of any person, society or religion. The film is at most 5 minutes (a film over the limit can be rejected) and at least 30 seconds. Do not show a credit list. A film shown in another competition or festival is not accepted, and if it is found later it is disqualified and its prize is withdrawn. Shoot in MPEG4 or AVI format (recommended ratios 16:9 or 16:9 Full Height Anamorphic, in DV or HDV). Students may do the direction, script, dialogue, lyrics, music, camera, light, art direction and editing, or invite outside persons, but due credit must be given when students did them. The organizers keep the non-exclusive right to show the film at any level and for non-commercial use, and to send it to national or international short film festivals. The organizers are not responsible for unauthorized use by a third party. A submitted film cannot be withdrawn. The host university screens all the films. First, Second and Third prizes are declared and given at the Prize Distribution Ceremony. The film in the first rank is sent by the host university to a national or international short film festival for the Indradhanushya. It is judged on content originality (story and script), production (camera, lighting, shot composition), post-production (editing, transitions, pacing, continuity, flow), image (focus, colour, lighting) and sound quality (clarity, level, no noise). Three copies of the subject or theme are given in Marathi, Hindi or English.","Procession (group event, not in this template): a cultural procession of the contingents is held on the first day, before the Inaugural Ceremony. All participating universities and their student participants must take part. The team should preferably show a theme of national or social importance, or the regional cultural tradition or features of the university. The team carries the university flag. It is judged on theme, costumes, presentation, overall impact and similar points. Three copies of the subject or theme are given in Marathi, Hindi or English."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Guidelines for the Indradhanushya (DBATU)","Url":"https://dbatu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Guidelines-for-the-Indradhanushaya-2023.pdf"}]}`),i=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Guidelines p.4-11 event rules",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each participating university sends only 1 student participant in each individual event."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each participating university sends only 1 student participant in each individual event.`}],a=[],o=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Indian Classical Vocal Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.4 Music (i); p.15 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","At most 2 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the details of the Raag, Taal and Bandish, written in Marathi, Hindi or English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the choice of raga, the presentation and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the details of the Raag, Taal and Bandish, written in Marathi, Hindi or English.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the choice of raga, the presentation and the general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Instrumental Percussion Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.4 Music (ii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","Only one accompanist.","Bring your own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are the choice of taal, the presentation and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- Only one accompanist.\\n- Bring your own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the choice of taal, the presentation and the general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Instrumental Non-Percussion Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.4 Music (iii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.","Only one accompanist.","Bring your own instruments."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are swar, taal, the choice of raga and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Present the item in either Hindustani or Karnataki style.\\n- Only one accompanist.\\n- Bring your own instruments.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are swar, taal, the choice of raga and the general impression."},{"Title":"Natyasangeet Vocal Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.4-5 Music (iv); p.15 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 5 to 7 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Present a song (natyapad) from any theatre tradition of India.","The song must be in the natyageet style. Any other type of song (Ovi or Bhavgeet) is not counted as natyageet.","At most 2 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song (natyapad) written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of its meaning in Marathi, Hindi or English if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi."],"Allowed":["Natyapad from films."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are sur, taal and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 5 to 7 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Present a song (natyapad) from any theatre tradition of India.\\n- The song must be in the natyageet style. Any other type of song (Ovi or Bhavgeet) is not counted as natyageet.\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song (natyapad) written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of its meaning in Marathi, Hindi or English if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Natyapad from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are sur, taal and the general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Light Vocal Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.5 Music (v); p.15 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 4 to 6 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["At most 2 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of its meaning if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are swara, taal and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 4 to 6 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of its meaning if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are swara, taal and the general impression."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.6 Music (viii); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 4 to 6 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Sing in English only.","You may sing any number of songs. There is no limit.","At most 2 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song or songs in English, and three copies of the meaning of the song or songs in English."],"Allowed":["A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument, by the student or the accompanists.","Film songs."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are the choice of songs, pitch, rhythm and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 4 to 6 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Sing in English only.\\n- You may sing any number of songs. There is no limit.\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song or songs in English, and three copies of the meaning of the song or songs in English.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A synthesizer or any other electronic instrument, by the student or the accompanists.\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the choice of songs, pitch, rhythm and the general impression."},{"Title":"Western Instrumental Solo","Source":"Guidelines p.6 Music (ix)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 5 to 7 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Play western music on any western percussion or non-percussion instrument.","Perform one genre or style, or fuse different genres or styles of western music.","At most 2 accompanists."],"Allowed":["The accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are rhythm, harmony and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 5 to 7 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Play western music on any western percussion or non-percussion instrument.\\n- Perform one genre or style, or fuse different genres or styles of western music.\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The accompanists may use a synthesizer or any other electronic instrument.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are rhythm, harmony and the general impression."},{"Title":"Indian Classical Dance","Source":"Guidelines p.6-7 Dance (i); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 12 to 15 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Perform one of the Indian classical dances: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam or Odissi.","At most 3 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of a synopsis in Marathi, Hindi or English on the dance and the dance story used in the accompanying song (if any), and three copies of the meaning of the song or songs in Marathi, Hindi or English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Classical style dances from films."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are taal, abhinaya or expressions, costumes, footwork and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 12 to 15 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Perform one of the Indian classical dances: Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniattam or Odissi.\\n- At most 3 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of a synopsis in Marathi, Hindi or English on the dance and the dance story used in the accompanying song (if any), and three copies of the meaning of the song or songs in Marathi, Hindi or English.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Classical style dances from films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are taal, abhinaya or expressions, costumes, footwork and the general impression."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Guidelines p.7 Literary (i)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Speak in Marathi, Hindi or English.","The subject or topic is announced in the meeting of Team Managers.","Speak in prose, not in poetry or song."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from a paper."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the introduction, the knowledge or study of the subject, the presentation, the language style and the overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Speak in Marathi, Hindi or English.\\n- The subject or topic is announced in the meeting of Team Managers.\\n- Speak in prose, not in poetry or song.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from a paper.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the introduction, the knowledge or study of the subject, the presentation, the language style and the overall effect."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Guidelines p.8 Theatre (i)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["You may mimic the sounds of machines and characters, and the speeches of well-known personalities."],"Allowed":["Naming the character on the stage."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are the skill of imitation, the variety of sounds and voices and the presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- You may mimic the sounds of machines and characters, and the speeches of well-known personalities.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Naming the character on the stage.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the skill of imitation, the variety of sounds and voices and the presentation."},{"Title":"On the Spot Painting","Source":"Guidelines p.9 Fine Arts (i)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Paint on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","The paper is half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the paper.","Paint in water, poster or pastel colours.","Bring your own materials, such as brushes and paints."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, composition, colour application, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Paint on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- The paper is half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the paper.\\n- Paint in water, poster or pastel colours.\\n- Bring your own materials, such as brushes and paints.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, composition, colour application, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"Guidelines p.9-10 Fine Arts (ii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Make a collage on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","The paper is half imperial size mount board, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the mount board.","Make the collage from old magazines. The host university gives the old magazines.","Bring your own pasting and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Make a collage on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- The paper is half imperial size mount board, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the mount board.\\n- Make the collage from old magazines. The host university gives the old magazines.\\n- Bring your own pasting and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Guidelines p.10 Fine Arts (iii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Make a poster on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","The paper is half imperial size mount board, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the mount board.","Make the poster in water, poster or pastel colours.","Bring your own materials, such as brushes, paints and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, presentation, tagline and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Make a poster on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- The paper is half imperial size mount board, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the mount board.\\n- Make the poster in water, poster or pastel colours.\\n- Bring your own materials, such as brushes, paints and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, presentation, tagline and overall impact."},{"Title":"Clay Modeling","Source":"Guidelines p.10 Fine Arts (iv)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Make a clay model on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","The host university gives the clay.","Bring your own materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Make a clay model on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- The host university gives the clay.\\n- Bring your own materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Guidelines p.10 Fine Arts (v)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Make a cartoon on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","The paper is half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the paper.","Bring your own materials, such as brushes, paints and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, characters, synchronization, colour application, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Make a cartoon on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- The paper is half imperial size drawing paper, 22 inches long and 15 inches wide. The host university gives the paper.\\n- Bring your own materials, such as brushes, paints and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, characters, synchronization, colour application, composition, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Guidelines p.11 Fine Arts (vi)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The event is held on the spot. Make a rangoli on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.","A space of 120 cm x 120 cm is given to the participant.","Use only rangoli powder and coloured powders.","Bring your own materials, such as white rangoli, coloured powder and other materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, colour scheme, elements, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The event is held on the spot. Make a rangoli on the subject given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- A space of 120 cm x 120 cm is given to the participant.\\n- Use only rangoli powder and coloured powders.\\n- Bring your own materials, such as white rangoli, coloured powder and other materials.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, colour scheme, elements, presentation and overall impact."},{"Title":"Spot Photography","Source":"Guidelines p.11 Fine Arts (vii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["Bring your own digital camera. Its memory card is formatted by the judges before the event starts.","Submit only your 5 best photographs on the subject, topic or theme given by the In-charge of the event.","More instructions are announced when the event starts.","The organizers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they like."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.","Software such as Photoshop or Picasa to improve the images."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Bring your own digital camera. Its memory card is formatted by the judges before the event starts.\\n- Submit only your 5 best photographs on the subject, topic or theme given by the In-charge of the event.\\n- More instructions are announced when the event starts.\\n- The organizers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they like.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Mixing, matching or morphing of photographs.\\n- Software such as Photoshop or Picasa to improve the images.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Indian Group Song","Source":"Guidelines p.5 Music (vi); p.15 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Total time for both songs: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 4 to 6 student participants.","Present two songs: one patriotic song and one Indian folk song.","The songs can be in any regional or official language of India.","At most 3 accompanists. The singers may play instruments while singing.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the songs written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the meaning if a song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs."],"Judging":["The judging is on composition, the choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Total time for both songs: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 4 to 6 student participants.\\n- Present two songs: one patriotic song and one Indian folk song.\\n- The songs can be in any regional or official language of India.\\n- At most 3 accompanists. The singers may play instruments while singing.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the songs written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of the meaning if a song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judging is on composition, the choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"Guidelines p.5 Music (vii); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 8 to 10 minutes. This does not include the time for setting or tuning the instruments.","An extra 10 minutes is given for setting or tuning the instruments before the event starts."],"Rules":["A team of 6 to 9 student participants.","At most 3 accompanists. They wear a different dress from the student participants, so that they can be easily seen as accompanists.","The accompanists sit or stand apart from the participants and do not lead the team.","Present original folk tunes of Maharashtra. The instruments must be original for that folk tune and suit the folk art of Maharashtra.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the synopsis written in Marathi, Hindi or English."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Folk tunes played in films."],"Judging":["The judging is on originality, composition, synchronization and variety. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 8 to 10 minutes. This does not include the time for setting or tuning the instruments.\\n- An extra 10 minutes is given for setting or tuning the instruments before the event starts.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 6 to 9 student participants.\\n- At most 3 accompanists. They wear a different dress from the student participants, so that they can be easily seen as accompanists.\\n- The accompanists sit or stand apart from the participants and do not lead the team.\\n- Present original folk tunes of Maharashtra. The instruments must be original for that folk tune and suit the folk art of Maharashtra.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the synopsis written in Marathi, Hindi or English.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Folk tunes played in films.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judging is on originality, composition, synchronization and variety. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Western Group Song","Source":"Guidelines p.6 Music (x); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Total time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 4 to 6 student participants.","Sing in English only.","The team may present any number of songs. There is no limit.","At most 3 accompanists. The singers may play western instruments while singing.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song or songs in English, and three copies of the meaning in English."],"Allowed":["Film songs."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judging is on composition, the choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Total time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 4 to 6 student participants.\\n- Sing in English only.\\n- The team may present any number of songs. There is no limit.\\n- At most 3 accompanists. The singers may play western instruments while singing.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the song or songs in English, and three copies of the meaning in English.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Film songs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judging is on composition, the choice of songs, synchronization, quality of singing, presentation and overall impact. It is not on the make-up, costumes and actions of the team."},{"Title":"Indian Folk Dance","Source":"Guidelines p.7 Dance (ii); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Total time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes.","Remove the sets, properties and instruments within 2 minutes after the performance."],"Rules":["A team of 8 to 10 student participants.","The dance must be a primitive Indian tribal dance or a folk dance. It must not be a classical dance.","At most 5 accompanists.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of a synopsis on the type or style of the dance, three copies of the song, and three copies of the meaning of the song, each in Marathi, Hindi or English (the meaning is needed if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Dances and folk dances from films.","Recorded music during the performance."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are originality, authenticity, music, rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Total time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 5 minutes.\\n- Remove the sets, properties and instruments within 2 minutes after the performance.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 8 to 10 student participants.\\n- The dance must be a primitive Indian tribal dance or a folk dance. It must not be a classical dance.\\n- At most 5 accompanists.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of a synopsis on the type or style of the dance, three copies of the song, and three copies of the meaning of the song, each in Marathi, Hindi or English (the meaning is needed if the song is in another language than Marathi or Hindi).\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Dances and folk dances from films.\\n- Recorded music during the performance.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are originality, authenticity, music, rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up and overall effect."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Guidelines p.7-8 Literary (ii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 2 student participants.","The proposition for the debate is announced in the meeting of Team Managers.","The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.","Each student speaks in Marathi, Hindi or English. Both can use the same language or different languages, but one student speaks in only one language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Reading from a paper."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the introduction, the knowledge or study of the subject, the presentation, the language style and the overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each student speaks for 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 2 student participants.\\n- The proposition for the debate is announced in the meeting of Team Managers.\\n- The first student speaks FOR the proposition and the second student speaks AGAINST it.\\n- Each student speaks in Marathi, Hindi or English. Both can use the same language or different languages, but one student speaks in only one language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Reading from a paper.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the introduction, the knowledge or study of the subject, the presentation, the language style and the overall effect."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"Guidelines p.8 Literary (iii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The Preliminary Round has 15 minutes for writing the answers."],"Rules":["A team of 3 student participants.","The competition has two rounds: a Preliminary Round and a Final Round.","In the Preliminary Round the team writes the answers to objective type questions. All the questions are in English only.","At most 6 teams are selected from the Preliminary Round for the Final Round, on merit.","The Final Round is oral, in an audio-visual format.","The Referee announces the special rules for the Final Round, the evaluation system, the time to answer a question and the steps of the round when the Final Round starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The Preliminary Round has 15 minutes for writing the answers.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 3 student participants.\\n- The competition has two rounds: a Preliminary Round and a Final Round.\\n- In the Preliminary Round the team writes the answers to objective type questions. All the questions are in English only.\\n- At most 6 teams are selected from the Preliminary Round for the Final Round, on merit.\\n- The Final Round is oral, in an audio-visual format.\\n- The Referee announces the special rules for the Final Round, the evaluation system, the time to answer a question and the steps of the round when the Final Round starts."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"Guidelines p.8 Theatre (ii); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 25 to 30 minutes.","Time to arrange the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Time to take them down: 5 minutes after the play."],"Rules":["A team of 2 to 9 student participants.","At most 3 accompanists.","The team brings its own set and stage property and make-up material. The host university can give lights and general property such as ordinary furniture if it is told in advance.","The play can be in prose or in verse.","The participating university must get all the permissions and censor certificates that are needed.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the script written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of a synopsis of the script in Marathi, Hindi or English if the script is in another language than Marathi or Hindi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Box sets."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the theme, acting, direction and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 25 to 30 minutes.\\n- Time to arrange the set and light: 10 minutes before the play. Time to take them down: 5 minutes after the play.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 2 to 9 student participants.\\n- At most 3 accompanists.\\n- The team brings its own set and stage property and make-up material. The host university can give lights and general property such as ordinary furniture if it is told in advance.\\n- The play can be in prose or in verse.\\n- The participating university must get all the permissions and censor certificates that are needed.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the script written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of a synopsis of the script in Marathi, Hindi or English if the script is in another language than Marathi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Box sets.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the theme, acting, direction and the general impression."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"Guidelines p.9 Theatre (iii); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 4 to 6 student participants.","At most 3 accompanists.","The skit should preferably show a theme of national or social importance.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity and bitter insinuations.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the script written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of a synopsis of the script if the script is in another language than Marathi or Hindi."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the theme, acting, co-ordination and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 4 to 6 student participants.\\n- At most 3 accompanists.\\n- The skit should preferably show a theme of national or social importance.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected. Avoid vulgarity and bitter insinuations.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the script written in Marathi, Hindi or English, and three copies of a synopsis of the script if the script is in another language than Marathi or Hindi.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the theme, acting, co-ordination and the general impression."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Guidelines p.9 Theatre (iv); p.16 documents","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time: 4 to 5 minutes.","Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 4 to 6 student participants.","The participants wear white or black skin-tight dresses and have painted faces with raised eyebrows and broadened lips.","At most 2 accompanists.","The concept must be shown only through expressions and gestures.","Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the theme written in Marathi, Hindi or English."],"Allowed":["Music, to strengthen the performance."],"NotAllowed":["Any property."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are the idea, the creativity of the presentation, the use of make-up and the general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time: 4 to 5 minutes.\\n- Time for stage or instrument setting: at most 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 4 to 6 student participants.\\n- The participants wear white or black skin-tight dresses and have painted faces with raised eyebrows and broadened lips.\\n- At most 2 accompanists.\\n- The concept must be shown only through expressions and gestures.\\n- Documents for the Event In-charge: three copies of the theme written in Marathi, Hindi or English.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Music, to strengthen the performance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any property.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are the idea, the creativity of the presentation, the use of make-up and the general impression."},{"Title":"Installation","Source":"Guidelines p.11 Fine Arts (viii)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["A team of 3 to 4 student participants.","Install or create an atmosphere on the subject, title or theme that the In-charge of the event announces on the spot.","Make only one installation, not bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet.","Compose or create your own image with the raw material."],"Allowed":["All materials used in other art forms such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modeling.","Waste material found in the surroundings, or any material brought from outside."],"NotAllowed":["Ready-made images or forms available in the market."],"Judging":["The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, synchronization, composition, presentation and overall impact."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Time to finish: not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A team of 3 to 4 student participants.\\n- Install or create an atmosphere on the subject, title or theme that the In-charge of the event announces on the spot.\\n- Make only one installation, not bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet.\\n- Compose or create your own image with the raw material.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- All materials used in other art forms such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modeling.\\n- Waste material found in the surroundings, or any material brought from outside.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Ready-made images or forms available in the market.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The qualities judged are visualization, delivery of the subject, handling of the medium, synchronization, composition, presentation and overall impact."}]'),s=[],r=[{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which the age is counted",Value:"30 September of the academic year in which the festival is held",Source:"Guidelines p.1 Rules of Eligibility 3"},{Key:"RegistrationPeriod",Kind:"date",Label:"Online registration dates",Value:"24th October to 31st October",Source:"Guidelines p.14 Guidelines 6 (printed without a year)"},{Key:"ProRataDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to pay the pro-rata amount",Value:"10th October",Source:"Guidelines p.14 Guidelines 8 (printed without a year)"},{Key:"TravelPlanNotice",Kind:"text",Label:"When to send the travel plan",Value:"5 days before the festival starts",Source:"Guidelines p.14 Guidelines 11"},{Key:"ProRataAmount",Kind:"fee",Label:"Pro-rata amount",Value:"Rs. 4 per student, or the revised pro-rata if there is one",Source:"Guidelines p.14 Guidelines 8"},{Key:"CautionMoney",Kind:"fee",Label:"Refundable caution money",Value:"Rs. 2000 (Guidelines to Universities, point 17). The Other Rules, point 2, print Rs. 1000 for each team",Source:"Guidelines p.3 Other Rules 2; p.14 Guidelines 17"},{Key:"ContingentSize",Kind:"text",Label:"Contingent details",Value:"The table of contingent details is: students including accompanists 49, Director Students' Development or Welfare 1, Cultural Co-ordinator or Official 1, Team Manager (male) 1, Team Manager (female) 1, Administrative staff 2, total 55",Source:"Guidelines p.2 Details of Contingent"}],l=[{Claim:"The eligibility, contingent, conduct, registration, fee, time and per-event rules are those of the Guidelines for the Indradhanushya: Maharashtra State Inter-University Youth Festival (2023).",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own guidelines",Source:"Guidelines for the Indradhanushya (2023), DBATU (16 pages)",Url:"https://dbatu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Guidelines-for-the-Indradhanushaya-2023.pdf"},{Claim:"The guidelines print no festival dates, host, venue, contacts, prizes (except Short Film placings), marks, points, grades or ranks, so these sections are left empty. Nothing was written from general knowledge.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own guidelines",Source:"Guidelines for the Indradhanushya (2023), DBATU",Url:"https://dbatu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Guidelines-for-the-Indradhanushaya-2023.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2023,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,u as default};
